        <div class="recent-updates-box">
            <time class="recent-updates-date"> Last update: Jul 2026 </time>
          <ol class="updates-list">
            
            <li class="updates-list-item">
              <time class="updates-list-date"> Jul 2026 </time>
              
              <h4 class="updates-list-heading">27 Underground Parking Facilities to Combat Mumbai&#39;s Parking Crisis</h4>
              
              <p class="updates-list-description">Mumbai is set to develop 27 underground parking facilities, one in each administrative ward, to alleviate the severe parking shortage. This project, backed by the BMC Budget 2026-27, will create parking beneath existing gardens and playgrounds, reducing roadside parking and traffic congestion. </p>
            </li>
            
            <li class="updates-list-item">
              <time class="updates-list-date"> Jun 2026 </time>
              
              <h4 class="updates-list-heading">New Road Link Approved to Enhance Mumbai Connectivity</h4>
              
              <p class="updates-list-description">The Maharashtra government has approved a ₹1,722 crore road link project aimed at connecting the Versova-Bandra Sea Link with the Mumbai Coastal Road. This infrastructure development is expected to significantly improve traffic flow, reduce commuting times across the city.</p>
            </li>
            
            <li class="updates-list-item">
              <time class="updates-list-date"> Jun 2026 </time>
              
              <p class="updates-list-description">Rent in Maryland CHS Worli ranges from ₹ 1 L to ₹ 1 L with options available for 2 BHK.</p>
            </li>
            
            <li class="updates-list-item">
              <time class="updates-list-date"> Jun 2026 </time>
              
              <p class="updates-list-description">During Q2&#39;2026, average property prices for Maryland CHS Worli moved from ₹ 51,200/sqft to ₹ 52,250/sqft, reflecting a 2.05% rise.</p>
            </li>
            
            <li class="updates-list-item">
              <time class="updates-list-date"> Apr 2026 </time>
              
              <h4 class="updates-list-heading">Mumbai to Establish Four New Helipads for Emergency Services</h4>
              
              <p class="updates-list-description">Mumbai authorities are planning to construct four new helipads within the next six years to enhance emergency response capabilities. Two helipads will be built along the Coastal Road, one at Worli and another in Kandivali&#39;s Charkop area. The remaining two will be developed in the Bandra Kurla Complex (BKC). </p>
            </li>
            
            <li class="updates-list-item">
              <time class="updates-list-date"> Apr 2026 </time>
              
              <h4 class="updates-list-heading">Elphinstone Road Overbridge Dismantled for Infrastructure Upgrade</h4>
              
              <p class="updates-list-description">Mumbai&#39;s historic Elphinstone Road Overbridge, a 113-year-old British-era structure, has been dismantled. This move is part of infrastructure upgrades aimed at improving rail operations and commuter safety. The dismantling creates space for two additional suburban lines between Kurla and Parel, which will eventually extend to CSMT. A new double-decker ROB will replace the old structure.</p>
            </li>
            
            <li class="updates-list-item">
              <time class="updates-list-date"> Mar 2026 </time>
              
              <h4 class="updates-list-heading">Versova Property Market Poised for Growth Driven by Sea Link and Redevelopment</h4>
              
              <p class="updates-list-description">The Versova property market is experiencing a surge in demand and property prices, fueled by the upcoming Versova-Bandra Sea Link and ongoing redevelopment projects. This infrastructure development is expected to sustain property values and attract significant buyer interest in the coming years.</p>
            </li>
            
            <li class="updates-list-item">
              <time class="updates-list-date"> Mar 2026 </time>
              
              <p class="updates-list-description">During Q1&#39;2026, average property prices for Maryland CHS Worli moved from ₹ 46,900/sqft to ₹ 51,200/sqft, reflecting a 9.17% rise.</p>
            </li>
            
            <li class="updates-list-item">
              <time class="updates-list-date"> Feb 2026 </time>
              
              <h4 class="updates-list-heading">Mumbai Infrastructure Projects Gain Momentum with Budget Allocations and Project Launches</h4>
              
              <p class="updates-list-description">Mumbai is experiencing a surge in infrastructure and activity. The BMC has proposed a record budget of ₹80,952.56 crore for FY 2026-27, with a significant portion allocated to infrastructure projects like the Coastal Road, Goregaon-Mulund Link Road (GMLR), and Sewage Treatment Plants (STPs).MMRDA has allocated over ₹5,400 crore for road tunnel projects, including one connecting Worli-Bandra Sea Link to Mumbai Airport.</p>
            </li>
            
            <li class="updates-list-item">
              <time class="updates-list-date"> Jan 2026 </time>
              
              <h4 class="updates-list-heading">BMC Outlines Timelines for Key Infrastructure Projects</h4>
              
              <p class="updates-list-description">The BMC has set completion targets for key infrastructure projects: the Bandra (E)-Kalanagar skywalk (almost complete) , the first phase of the Bandra-Dharavi flyover reconstruction (Mithi river widening project ,near completion) , and the Worli connector by December 2026. These projects are expected to improve pedestrian access, ease traffic congestion, and enhance overall connectivity within the city.</p>
            </li>
            
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    
    
  
</section>


      




      
      

      

      


      



      

